; EdSharp.inix -- the SHIPPED configuration layer, read from the program
; folder. Entries here override the same [Section] Key in EdSharp.ini,
; and the installer refreshes this file on every upgrade -- so do not
; put personal settings here. For personal overrides, create an
; EdSharp.inix next to your EdSharp.ini in EdSharp's data folder; that
; user layer outranks this file, which outranks both .ini files.
; An EMPTY value here is a tombstone: it disables and hides that entry
; everywhere, including stale copies in a user's old EdSharp.ini.
;
; Conversion policy, applied 23 August 2026:
;   * Pandoc does every conversion it supports, called directly.
;   * When Pandoc cannot read a format (old Word .doc, PDF, PowerPoint,
;     Excel), 2htm.exe or the OfficeConvert utilities do the work,
;     through .cmd batch files in Convert (never .bat).
;   * Entries whose tools are gone from Convert are tombstoned:
;     braille (liblouis), HTML Tidy, WinHelp and WordPerfect (GetText),
;     and the epub32 entries that never had a Pandoc reader.
;   * pdf2txt now uses 2htm (Word's PDF Reflow) since Xpdf is gone.
;   * Updated 24 August 2026: Pandoc 3.8.3 added pptx and xlsx READERS,
;     so pptx2* and xlsx2* imports now call pandoc.exe directly and the
;     middleware for them is retired. installPandoc keeps Pandoc
;     current, so no version gating is needed. Bridges remain only
;     where Pandoc has no reader or writer: legacy .doc/.ppt/.xls and
;     PDF still go through 2htm or OfficeConvert, xls2md still builds
;     its CSV with OfficeConvert (sheet2md.cmd), and xlsx2csv keeps
;     XlVert because Pandoc has no CSV writer. New in the same spirit:
;     AsciiDoc (adoc) and typst (typ) imports, an md2pptx export, and
;     md2docxrefs, which runs --citeproc for citation-ready Word
;     output (see Pandoc_Office_Guide.md).
;   * Also 24 August 2026: the .inix TABLE conversions. inixVert.exe
;     (built from the shared Inix.cs) moves tabular data between
;     .inix, .csv, .tsv, .md, and .xlsx in pure .NET -- no Office, no
;     ACE. Import: csv2inix, md2inix, xlsx2inix. Export: inix2csv,
;     inix2md, inix2xlsx. xlsx2csv also uses it now, so that
;     conversion no longer needs Office either.
;   * The .mdx format (Markdown with embedded inix tables): a fenced
;     code block whose info string is "inix" holds records the
;     field = value way, and expansion turns each block into a real
;     Markdown table (a grid table when cells are multi-line) before
;     pandoc renders docx or HTML. mdx2md shows the expansion;
;     mdx2htm and mdx2docx chain it with pandoc. A block's optional
;     [Global] section may set caption and fields; with no Global,
;     every field appears in first-seen order.
;   * PANDOC IS FOUND ON THE PATH, NOT KEPT IN THIS FOLDER (26 September
;     2026). Every conversion says plain "pandoc". Shared components --
;     Pandoc, Python, Node, Ollama -- install machine-wide to their own
;     default folders so every Homer program shares one copy, and an app
;     upgrade, which replaces the app's folder, cannot destroy them. A
;     beta tester who already had Pandoc through Chocolatey was given a
;     second copy inside EdSharp's folder; that is what this ends.
;   * The md2htm and md2html EXPORTS carry --mathml (was --mathjax from
;     24 August 2026, changed 30 August 2026): TeX math in Markdown
;     reaches the browser as real, screen-reader-accessible math.
;     MathML is now the better of the two and needs no script at all.
;     Every major browser has rendered MathML natively since MathML Core
;     reached Chromium in 2023; NVDA reads it from 2025.1 and has MathCAT
;     built in from 2026.1, needing no add-on, and JAWS reads it from its
;     2026 releases. MathJax meant fetching a large script from a content
;     network every time a page opened -- so no math offline -- and its
;     version 4 turned off the hidden MathML that screen readers had been
;     relying on, in favour of speech of its own. Native MathML is
;     smaller, works with no network, and is read by the screen reader
;     itself rather than by a script.
;   * New: HTML and Markdown targets for doc, pdf, ppt, and pptx via
;     any2htm.cmd (2htm reads the source and makes HTML; EdSharp's
;     built-in ReverseMarkdown converter then makes the Markdown --
;     the Markdown from it), and rtf2htm, rtf2md, rtf2txt via Pandoc's
;     RTF reader.
;   * The Compiler lines for MinGW C++ and PowerBASIC now call the
;     .cmd scripts; the .bat versions are retired.
;   * To style docx output, create a reference document and add, in
;     your data-folder EdSharp.inix, a docx line ending with:
;     --reference-doc "%DataDir%\reference.docx"
;   * PDF targets use Pandoc's documented method (the .pdf output
;     extension selects PDF) and need a LaTeX engine like MiKTeX.
[Import]
adoc2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f asciidoc -t html -s -o %Target%
adoc2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f asciidoc -t gfm -o %Target%
adoc2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f asciidoc -t plain -o %Target%
csv2inix=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\inixVert.exe "%SourceLong%" %Target% /quiet
doc2htm=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\any2htm.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
doc2html=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\any2htm.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
doc2md=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\any2htm.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
doc2txt=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
docx2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f docx -t html -s -o %Target%
docx2html=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f docx -t html -s -o %Target%
docx2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f docx -t gfm -o %Target%
docx2mw=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f docx -t mediawiki -o %Target%
docx2rst=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f docx -t rst -o %Target%
docx2tex=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f docx -t latex -s -o %Target%
docx2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f docx -t plain -o %Target%
epub2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f epub -t html -s -o %Target%
epub2html=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f epub -t html -s -o %Target%
epub2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f epub -t gfm -o %Target%
epub2mw=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f epub -t mediawiki -o %Target%
epub2tex=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f epub -t latex -s -o %Target%
epub2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f epub -t plain -o %Target%
htm2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t gfm -o %Target%
htm2mw=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t mediawiki -o %Target%
htm2rst=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t rst -o %Target%
htm2tex=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t latex -s -o %Target%
htm2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t plain -o %Target%
html2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t gfm -o %Target%
html2mw=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t mediawiki -o %Target%
html2rst=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t rst -o %Target%
html2tex=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t latex -s -o %Target%
html2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f html -t plain -o %Target%
md2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f gfm -t html -s -o %Target%
md2html=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f gfm -t html -s -o %Target%
md2mw=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f gfm -t mediawiki -o %Target%
md2rst=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f gfm -t rst -o %Target%
md2rtf=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f gfm -t rtf -s -o %Target%
md2tex=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f gfm -t latex -s -o %Target%
md2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f gfm -t plain -o %Target%
md2inix=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\inixVert.exe "%SourceLong%" %Target% /quiet
mdx2htm=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\mdx2htm.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
mdx2md=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\inixVert.exe "%SourceLong%" %Target% /quiet
odt2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f odt -t html -s -o %Target%
odt2html=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f odt -t html -s -o %Target%
odt2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f odt -t gfm -o %Target%
odt2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f odt -t plain -o %Target%
; PDF conversion goes one way for every target: pdf2md.cmd reads the
; PDF with the free PyMuPDF reader and writes RICH Markdown -- headings,
; lists, tables, emphasis -- and EdSharp turns that into HTML or plain
; text in the binary, or into a Word document with Pandoc. Nothing here
; needs Microsoft Word, and no target is a bare text dump.
pdf2htm=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\pdf2md.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
pdf2html=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\pdf2md.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
pdf2md=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\pdf2md.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
pdf2txt=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\pdf2md.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
ppt2htm=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\any2htm.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
ppt2md=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\any2htm.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
ppt2txt=%ProgDir%\configs\convert\any2txt.cmd "%ProgDirLong%" "%SourceLong%" "%TargetLong%"
pptx2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f pptx -t html -s -o %Target%
pptx2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f pptx -t gfm -o %Target%
pptx2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f pptx -t plain -o %Target%
rst2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rst -t html -s -o %Target%
rst2html=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rst -t html -s -o %Target%
rst2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rst -t gfm -o %Target%
rst2mw=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rst -t mediawiki -o %Target%
rst2tex=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rst -t latex -s -o %Target%
rst2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rst -t plain -o %Target%
rtf2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rtf -t html -s -o %Target%
rtf2html=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rtf -t html -s -o %Target%
rtf2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rtf -t gfm -o %Target%
rtf2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f rtf -t plain -o %Target%
typ2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f typst -t html -s -o %Target%
typ2md=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f typst -t gfm -o %Target%
typ2txt=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f typst -t plain -o %Target%
tex2htm=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f latex -t html -s -o %Target%
tex2html=pandoc "%SourceLong%" -f latex -t html -s -o %Target%
